Description: panfrost: fix MTK 16L32S detiling before Valhall
 Before Valhall, shader images are bound as attribute buffers whose S/T
 dimensions are taken from the pipe_resource. For the tiled sources of the
 MTK detile compute shader that is the size of the detiled plane, while the
 shader reads the one-tile-per-row view that the import set up (extent_px,
 e.g. 128x4080 texels for a 1920x1088 luma plane). Loads beyond the plane
 height were out of bounds and returned zero: only the first <height> luma
 tiles and <height/2> chroma tiles were copied, the rest of the picture
 stayed black/green. Seen on Mali-G76 (Bifrost v7) with the MT6785 video
 decoder (MM21 output) through EGL dma-buf import, e.g. GStreamer glupload.
 Expose the size of the tiled view while the images are bound and restore
 height0 together with width0 afterwards.
Author: pocket-debs
Forwarded: no
License: MIT (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
@@ -4074,6 +4074,23 @@ panfrost_mtk_detile_compute(struct panfr
          DIV_ROUND_UP(uv_src->height0, 16);
    }
 
+   /* Before Valhall, images are bound as attribute buffers whose S/T
+    * dimensions come from the pipe_resource. For the tiled sources that is
+    * the size of the detiled plane, but the shader reads the one-tile-per-row
+    * view set up at import (extent_px), which has far more rows: loads past
+    * the plane height would be out of bounds and return zero, leaving the
+    * lower part of the destination black. Expose the view size while the
+    * images are bound; panfrost_resource_restore_format() puts it back. */
+   if (y_src) {
+      y_src->width0 = pan_resource(y_src)->image.props.extent_px.width;
+      y_src->height0 = pan_resource(y_src)->image.props.extent_px.height;
+   }
+
+   if (uv_src) {
+      uv_src->width0 = pan_resource(uv_src)->image.props.extent_px.width;
+      uv_src->height0 = pan_resource(uv_src)->image.props.extent_px.height;
+   }
+
    image[0].resource = y_src;
    image[0].format = PIPE_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UINT;
    image[0].shader_access = image[0].access = PIPE_IMAGE_ACCESS_READ;
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -1263,6 +1263,7 @@ panfrost_resource_restore_format(struct
    rsrc->base.format = saved->base.format;
    rsrc->image.props.format = saved->image.props.format;
    rsrc->base.width0 = saved->base.width0;
+   rsrc->base.height0 = saved->base.height0;
    rsrc->image.props.extent_px.width = saved->image.props.extent_px.width;
    rsrc->image.props.extent_px.height = saved->image.props.extent_px.height;
 }
